# CL-CHK-001-v1.0 — TIER-1 (GP-AUTO-034) ACTIVATION GATE CHECKLIST

**Author:** CL-01, 2026-07-23. **Class:** prep checklist (allowed pre-activation). For GP to work through to bring register/surface automation to activation-ready. Activation still requires the operator's §13 sentence.

Each gate must be recorded (with evidence) before the next matters:

- [ ] **G1.** Byte-exact, reconstructable executable source published; exact source hash recorded.
- [ ] **G2.** Installed-source hash == published source hash (verified).
- [ ] **G3.** ≥2 non-author source reviews filed, evidence lineage disclosed (per the class independence standard).
- [ ] **G4.** Test suite ALL-PASS: injection, rejected-injection, revocation, retention, hard-kill, recovery, rollback.
- [ ] **G5.** Google-runtime acceptance + inspected live-run receipt (shadow mode).
- [ ] **G6.** No critical transition alarm.
- [ ] **G7.** Post-test **3-of-4** affirmative vote on the exact tested revision / source hash.
- [ ] **G8. (OPERATOR — direct entry only)** Dylan records: `APPROVE WRITE-CAPABLE TIER 1 UNDER OP-PROT-008-R0.1 FOR THE EXACT TESTED GP-AUTO-034 SOURCE HASH [HASH]. TIERS 2–4 RECEIVE NO ADDITIONAL WRITE AUTHORITY FROM THIS ACTIVATION.`

Until G8, Tier 1 is preparation/shadow-only and all fail-closed switches remain. Once active, Tier 1 may **only** reconcile surfaces (dashboards, START_HERE, queues, indexes) to trusted registers — never create math authority, terminalize, promote, replace machine roots, release, or delete (R0.1 §5.3).
